[h2]Steam Cards[/h2]
Now the game will reward you with [b]Trading Cards[/b] that can be collected to craft [i]Steam Badges[/i]. We are also adding other community items like [i]Backgrounds[/i] and [i]Emoticons[/i] in this update.

[h2]General Update[/h2]
[*]Stats will no longer show for bonuses that are equal to zero for better readability;
[*][i]Temporary Upgrades[/i] are slightly more likely to appear;
[*][i]Temporary Upgrades[/i] can appear on the 5th wave onwards (was between the waves 10 and 25);
[*]Whenever you reach the amount of cheese necessary to win a wave you automatically become invulnerable to prevent frustrating deaths due to unfortunate timing;
[*]Cheese to reach the wave threshold is now added immediately upon an enemy's death, instead of when the cheese is collected by you;
[*]Now, the [i]30th Wave[/i] will also grant you an upgrade;
[*][i]Curse Damage[/i] will also benefit from extra damage taken by enemies;
[*]New songs were added.

[h2]Upgrades Collection[/h2]
[*]The Upgrades Collection can now be scrolled through by clicking with the mouse.

[h2]Waves[/h2]
[*]Amount of cheese necessary on Waves 30+ decreased from [b]250[/b] to [b]50[/b].

[h2]Upgrades[/h2]
[h3]Changes[/h3]
[*][b]Ammo V[/b]: Increases projectile damage by [b]200%[/b] of your ammo (was [i]50%[/i]);
[*][b]Impact VI[/b]: Reduced shot spread by 30%.

[h3]New Upgrades[/h3]
[*][b]Star Arrow X[/b]: Your star allies can also summon arrows;
[*][b]Debuff Master X[/b]: Your debuff damage is increased by 100%. Your debuff speed is increased by 100%;

[*][b]Glass Heart ???[/b]: Your total amount of hearts are reduced to 1.0. Your total bonus projectile damage is multiplied by 2.0;
[*][b]Unalterable Critical ???[/b]: Your critical damage is always at 300%;
[*][b]Speed Transmutation ???[/b]: All your bonus movement speed is transformed into critical chance;
[*][b]Silver Bullet ???[/b]: Decreases your total ammo by 99%. Increases your projectile penetration by 9876%. Increases projectile damage by 250%;
[*][b]Cursed Cannons ???[/b]: Your reload time takes 2.0 times longer. Your number of shots is 3.0 times bigger.

[h2]Characters[/h2]
[h3]Mr. Lucky[/h3]
[*]Swapped some skills around the skill tree;

[*][i]Increases upgrade options and roll count by 1. Whenever you roll, your projectile damage and reload speed increase by 3%[/i] (REMOVED);

[*][i]During the waves of number: 5, 15, 25, you gain one extra upgrade[/i] (NEW);
[*][i]Increases upgrade options and roll count by 1[/i] (NEW);
[*][i]Whenever you roll, your projectile damage and reload speed increase by 3%[/i] (NEW);

[*][i]Increases projectile damage by 50%[/i] (was [i]20%[/i]);
[*][i]Increases the amount of cheese that enemies drop by 50%[/i] (was [i]Increases movement speed by 20%[/i]);
[*][i]Every 3 waves, randomly increase your projectile damage, fire rate, reload speed, ammo or critical damage by 25%[/i] (was [i]Increases projectile damage, fire rate, reload speed, ammo and critical damage by 25%[/i]);
[*][i]Increases critical damage by 50% for every rare upgrade you have[/i] (was [i]Increases projectile damage by 10% for every upgrade you have[/i]);

[h3]Soldier[/h3]
[*][i]Every 3 waves, you gain 40% extra ammo[/i] (was [i]Every 5 waves[/i]);
[*][i]Increases shot number by 3. Increases ammo by 100%. Whenever you kill 3 enemies, the 2 closest enemies die[/i] (was [i]Increases shot number by 3. Increases ammo by 40%[/i]);
[*][i]Increases fire rate by 50%. Increases reload speed by 40%. Whenever you kill 3 enemies, the 2 closest enemies die[/i] (was [i]Increases fire rate by 50%. Increases reload speed by 40%. Increases ammo by 30%[/i]).

[h3]Doctor[/h3]
[*][i]Your poison damage is increased by 50%. Your poison speed is increased by 50%[/i] (was [i]Every 5 waves, you gain 10% extra poison damage[/i]);
[*][i]Every 5 waves, you gain 50% poison speed[/i] (was [i]Your poison damage and poison speed is increased by 30% and 100%, respectively[/i]);
[*][i]Every 5 waves, you gain 50% poison damage[/i] (was [i]Your poison damage and poison speed is increased by 100% and 30%, respectively[/i]);
[*][i]Every 5 waves, you gain 40% extra curse speed[/i] (was [i]10%[/i]);
[*][i]Every 5 waves, cursed enemies take 50% extra damage[/i] (was [i]15%[/i]).

[h3]M1C3[/h3]
[*]Swapped some skills around the skill tree;

[*][i]Increases fire rate by 40%[/i] (REMOVED);
[*][i]You don't get upgrades for 5 waves. After that you get 3 upgrades for 5 waves[/i](REMOVED);

[*][i]Increases knockback by 100%[/i] (was [i]50%[/i]);
[*][i]Increases critical damage by 100%[/i] (was [i]50%[/i]);
[*][i]Gear upgrades are more likely to appear. Gear upgrades can show up repeatedly throughout a run. Gear upgrades will grant you additional upgrades on wave 20[/i] (was [i]After 5 waves, you get the Gear V and 2 extra upgrades[/i])
[*][i]Replaces all your hearts with metal hearts. For every metal half heart, increases your projectile damage and your projectile penetration by 60%[/i] (was [i]For every half heart missing[/i]);
[*][i]After standing still for 3 seconds, your gain 150% increased fire rate, and 150% arrow damage[/i] (was [i]100% and 150%[/i], respectively).

[h3]Mr. Shock[/h3]
[*] Swapped some skills around the skill tree;

[*][i]Every 20th hit to an enemy increases your lightning damage by 1%[/i] (was [i]Every 15th hit[/i]);
[*][i]Your lightnings area damage is 100% bigger in size[/i] (was [i]You summon 1 extra lightnings[/i])
[*][i]Increases fire rate by 50%[/i] (was [i]20%[/i]);
[*][i]Your lightnings also stun enemies for 0.8 seconds[/i] (was [i]for 0.5 seconds[/i]);
[*][i]Your lightning damage is increased by 50%. Increases fire rate by 50%.[/i] (was [i]20% and 20%[/i], respectively]);
[*][i]Every 8 waves, you summon 1 extra lightnings[/i] (was [i]Every 10 waves[/i]).

[h2]Bug Fixes[/h2]
[*]Fixed some localization issues;
[*]Fixed a bug where [i]Curse spread[/i] from the [i]Curse III Upgrade[/i] sometimes wouldn't spread.

[h2]General Update[/h2]
- Reduced the delay for the enemies to start showing up after selecting an upgrade;

- [b]Perfuration X[/b]: Now also increases projectile penetration of [i]Star Projectiles[/i] and [i]Arrow Projectiles[/i];

[h2]Bug Fixes[/h2]
- Fixed an issue where if you already had all the achievements you wouldn't be able to get the [i]Cheese Moon[/i] achievement;
- Fixed some localization issues;

[h2]General Update[/h2]
- Added a menu option to disable automatic pause when tabbed out;
- Added a menu option to restart a run;
- You can now see the [b]enemy health increase[/b] and [b]enemy speed increase[/b] in the stats menu along with your stat increases;
- You can now see the [b]shot number increase[/b] in the stats menu;
- Now the game will teach you how to show game stats for the first time;
- Added an achievement when you unlock all the achievements.

[h2]Waves 30+[/h2]
- Number of cheese necessary between waves decreased from [b]800[/b] to [b]250[/b];
- Enemy health and speed scaling decreased, and scale changed from linear to exponential.

[h2]Characters[/h2]
[h3]Mr. Shock[/h3]
- Your lightning damage is increased by 100% (was [i]20%[/i]);
- Every 15th hit to an enemy increases your lightning damage by 1% (was [i]Every 25th enemy killed increases your lightning damage by 1%[/i]).

[h2]Upgrades[/h2]
- [b]Gear Upgrades[/b] can now be collected in multiple quantities (before that, whenever you got a [i]Gear Upgrade[/i] it would no longer show up any of the other [i]Gear Upgrades[/i]).
- [b]Rare Upgrades[/b] are now named;
- [b]Rare Upgrades[/b] are now easier to find;
- [b]Combo Upgrades[/b] now have a unique card background and sound effect when showing up;

- [b]Curse III[/b]: Whenever you take damage or dodge, you inflict curse on all enemies nearby (now also spreads curse when successfully dodging);
- [b]Health V[/b]: Every 200th enemy killed heals you by 0.5 hearts (now only counts down enemies when not full on health);
- [b]Critical V[/b]: Hitting a critical shot empowers your next attack with a 60% increased critical damage (no longer caps at 1000% and swapped with [i]Critical VII[/i]);
- [b]Critical VII[/b]: Whenever a shot kills an enemy with a critical hit, it increases your next attack's shot number by 1 (swapped with [i]Critical V[/i]);
- [b]Overload[/b]: Increases all damage sources by 100% (was [i]Increases all damage sources by 40%[/i], and now also increases curse damage).

[h2]Bug Fixes[/h2]
- Fixed and issue where fully upgrading one skill tree then buying a single skill from other skill trees would incorrectly prompt you with an achievement;
- Fixed an issue where the game could crash when choosing upgrades with the arrow keys on the keyboard.

[h2]Dev Notes[/h2]
One of the most asked additions is finally here, which is an [b]Upgrade Collection[/b] to see whichever upgrades are left for [i]The Collector[/i] achievement. Aside from that, these are mostly a bunch of changes of quality life to make the experience better, a bit of balancing where it was needed, adjustments to the Waves beyond 30 that felt too frustrating way too quickly.

I also felt like adding an achievement to have all achievement was a good idea so whenever we have [i]Profile Features[/i] available for the game you'll be able to show it off on your profile. If you already have all the achievements and is missing this one, you just have to open the game and it should pop off.

I hope you folks enjoy it. I've been having a blast from the amount of love I've been receiving from you all playing the game so I felt the need to make this update live ASAP.

[h2]General Update[/h2]

Arrows no longer trigger Lightning, nor inflict Curse or Poison;
Lightnings no longer inflict Curse or Poison;
Star Allies no longer trigger Lightning, nor inflict Curse or Poison;

[b]Lightning V[/b]: Your lightnings target your closest enemies (swapped with [i]Lightning VII[/i]);
[b]Lightning VII[/b]: Your lightnings deal damage in an area of effect (swapped [i]with Lightning V[/i]);

The affected upgrades have updated descriptions to explain the new interactions.

[h2]New Upgrades[/h2]

[b]Lightning Arrow X[/b]: Your arrows can also summon lightnings;
[b]Poison Arrow X[/b]: Your arrows can also inflict poison;
[b]Curse Arrow X[/b]: Your arrows can also inflict curse;

[b]Poison Lightning X[/b]: Your lightnings can also inflict poison;
[b]Curse Lightning X[/b]: Your lightnings can also inflict curse;

[b]Lightning Star X[/b]: Your star allies can also summon lightnings;
[b]Poison Star X[/b]: Your star allies can also inflict poison;
[b]Curse Star X[/b]: Your star allies can also inflict curse;

All the above upgrades need their respective upgrades on maximum to show up; i.e: for [b]Lightning Arrow X[/b] to show up, you need both the [b]Arrow VII[/b] and [b]Lightning VII[/b] upgrades equipped.

[h3]A note from the Dev[/h3]
These changes were made to better clarify how the mechanics work while also adjusting them to feel more fair.

Before these changes you could pick the [b]Arrow V[/b] and [b]Lightning V[/b] upgrades and just be invincible for 80 waves straight, due to free chained synergy between them. 

Now with this update, these interactions will still be possible, but will be more difficult to achieve, needing a whole build around them for the upgrade that merges them together to appear, leading to a tougher early game that can still be facilitated through meta progression upgrades, more interesting builds and decisions, and not just pick-everything gameplay.
